window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"To guide the development team on what they intend to achieve, a product owner provides a table that includes the key deliverables of each quarter of the 9-month project. What artifact does this table represent?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sX\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product vision statement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Product vision statement\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product wireframe<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Product wireframe\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product roadmap<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Product roadmap\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product backlog<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Product backlog\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A product roadmap is a strategic plan that highlights the key components of a product that are scheduled for delivery across a portfolio, program, or several project iterations or releases, including the likely order in which these components will be delivered (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 55). The product roadmap indicates where the product is headed in both the short and long terms. In agile organizations, the product roadmap serves as a guide rather than a project plan<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A product vision statement outlines what a product would look like to ultimately achieve its vision and give purpose to its existence. A vision statement should be short, simple, and specific.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Product wireframe is a mockup or a sketch of the user interface, high-level functionality, page layout, etc. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The product roadmap is different from the product backlog in that the product roadmap provides the big picture while the product backlog tackles the practical and feasible steps required to tangibly create the product.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A product roadmap is a strategic plan that highlights the key components of a product that are scheduled for delivery across a portfolio, program, or several project iterations or releases, including the likely order in which these components will be delivered (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 55). The product roadmap indicates where the product is headed in both the short and long terms. In agile organizations, the product roadmap serves as a guide rather than a project plan . Option A: A product vision statement outlines what a product would look like to ultimately achieve its vision and give purpose to its existence. A vision statement should be short, simple, and specific. Option B: The Product wireframe is a mockup or a sketch of the user interface, high-level functionality, page layout, etc. Option D: The product roadmap is different from the product backlog in that the product roadmap provides the big picture while the product backlog tackles the practical and feasible steps required to tangibly create the product.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":6,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-1\\\">A business analyst is eager to implement a new solution for the company. The stakeholders requested an assessment of the business value it will bring. What should the business analyst do? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is eager to implement a new solution for the company. The stakeholders requested an assessment of the business value it will bring. What should the business analyst do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Conduct a cost-benefit analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Conduct a cost-benefit analysis\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use a benchmarking technique<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Use a benchmarking technique\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct a feasibility study<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Conduct a feasibility study\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Conduct a feature injection<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Conduct a feature injection\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A cost-benefit analysis evaluates the financial return of implementing the solution by comparing the expected benefits against the costs. It's an effective way to assess the business value of a solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Benchmarking typically involves comparing a company’s performance or processes to industry standards or best practices. While useful for understanding relative performance, it doesn't directly assess the specific business value of a new solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A feasibility study assesses whether a project or solution is viable and can be successfully implemented. It focuses more on the practicality of the solution rather than its business value.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Feature injection involves breaking down and analyzing features to understand their value and implementation. While this can help in understanding specific aspects of a solution, it doesn’t directly assess the overall business value.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A cost-benefit analysis evaluates the financial return of implementing the solution by comparing the expected benefits against the costs. It's an effective way to assess the business value of a solution. Option B: Benchmarking typically involves comparing a company’s performance or processes to industry standards or best practices. While useful for understanding relative performance, it doesn't directly assess the specific business value of a new solution. Option C: A feasibility study assesses whether a project or solution is viable and can be successfully implemented. It focuses more on the practicality of the solution rather than its business value. Option D: Feature injection involves breaking down and analyzing features to understand their value and implementation. While this can help in understanding specific aspects of a solution, it doesn’t directly assess the overall business value.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":7,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The project team finds out that several implemented features deviate from what is specified in the scope statement. Which document should the project manager consult to address the issue?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The project team finds out that several implemented features deviate from what is specified in the scope statement. Which document should the project manager consult to address the issue?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>WBS ​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. WBS\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>WBS dictionary​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. WBS dictionary\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>    <span><\\/span> <\\/span>Requirements traceability matrix<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Requirements traceability matrix\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Project charter<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Project charter\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The traceability Matrix is a document that maps requirements as well as other aspects of the project. It's used as evidence to confirm that requirements have been fulfilled, as it typically documents those requirements along with issues and test results (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 189).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The traceability Matrix is a document that maps requirements as well as other aspects of the project. It's used as evidence to confirm that requirements have been fulfilled, as it typically documents those requirements along with issues and test results (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 189).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":8,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sTU-0\\\">To validate requirements, a business analyst used a technique illustrated by the following graph. What technique did the business analyst use?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"To validate requirements, a business analyst used a technique illustrated by the following graph. What technique did the business analyst use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus Groups<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Focus Groups\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Nominal Group<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Nominal Group\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Brainstorming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Brainstorming\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Delphi<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Delphi\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Delphi is a consensus-building method that consolidates anonymous input from subject matter experts (SMEs) using rounds of voting (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 228).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Delphi is a consensus-building method that consolidates anonymous input from subject matter experts (SMEs) using rounds of voting (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 228).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":9,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A project team is actively working on creating a solution and preparing it for delivery to the business. In which phase of the project would this activity take place?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project team is actively working on creating a solution and preparing it for delivery to the business. In which phase of the project would this activity take place?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Execution<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Execution\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Planning<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Planning\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Monitoring and controlling<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Monitoring and controlling\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Closure<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Closure\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In the Execution Phase, the project team develops, implements, and delivers the solution to the business. This phase involves carrying out the work defined in the project plan, managing resources, and ensuring that the deliverables meet the project’s objectives.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Planning Phase involves creating detailed plans to guide the execution and control of the project. This includes defining tasks, schedules, budgets, resources, and risk management strategies. While crucial for setting up the project, this phase does not involve implementing or delivering the solution<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The Monitoring and Controlling phase involves tracking the project’s progress, ensuring it stays on track with the plan, and making adjustments as needed. This phase is about oversight and control rather than the active development or delivery of the solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The Closure Phase marks the formal completion of the project. In this phase, final deliverables are handed over, project documentation is completed, and a post-project review may be conducted. Although this phase may include the final delivery of the project outcome, it does not involve the actual development or implementation of the solution, which is done during the Execution Phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A In the Execution Phase, the project team develops, implements, and delivers the solution to the business. This phase involves carrying out the work defined in the project plan, managing resources, and ensuring that the deliverables meet the project’s objectives. Option B: The Planning Phase involves creating detailed plans to guide the execution and control of the project. This includes defining tasks, schedules, budgets, resources, and risk management strategies. While crucial for setting up the project, this phase does not involve implementing or delivering the solution . Option C: The Monitoring and Controlling phase involves tracking the project’s progress, ensuring it stays on track with the plan, and making adjustments as needed. This phase is about oversight and control rather than the active development or delivery of the solution. Option D: The Closure Phase marks the formal completion of the project. In this phase, final deliverables are handed over, project documentation is completed, and a post-project review may be conducted. Although this phase may include the final delivery of the project outcome, it does not involve the actual development or implementation of the solution, which is done during the Execution Phase.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":10,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">An organization has appointed a new project manager to replace the one who recently left. What should the new project manager do first?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization has appointed a new project manager to replace the one who recently left. What should the new project manager do first?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Check the issue log and the lessons learned register for any serious problems.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Check the issue log and the lessons learned register for any serious problems.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Check the project charter to understand the project’s goal and business case.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Check the project charter to understand the project’s goal and business case.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Check the project management plan to learn about the project baselines.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Check the project management plan to learn about the project baselines.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Check the stakeholders’ register to start interacting with the different parties involved in the project.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Check the stakeholders’ register to start interacting with the different parties involved in the project.\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">First and foremost, the project manager has to understand why the project is being created in the first place; aka its business case. Moreover, the project manager should be aware of the project’s predefined goals. These two elements along with the main deliverables are all defined in the project charter.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B First and foremost, the project manager has to understand why the project is being created in the first place; aka its business case. Moreover, the project manager should be aware of the project’s predefined goals. These two elements along with the main deliverables are all defined in the project charter.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":11,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A Business Analyst is tasked with developing a product roadmap for the upcoming project. What technique should the Business Analyst choose to develop the roadmap in order to ensure it effectively captures the sequence and prioritization of user stories?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A Business Analyst is tasked with developing a product roadmap for the upcoming project. What technique should the Business Analyst choose to develop the roadmap in order to ensure it effectively captures the sequence and prioritization of user stories?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use cas<span><\\/span>e<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Use cas e\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Story mapping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Story mapping\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SWOT analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. SWOT analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Wireframe<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Wireframe\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Story mapping is a technique for sequencing user stories based on their business value and the typical user sequence. It helps teams gain a shared understanding of the product to be built and communicates the features and components to be delivered. Initially, stories may be written at a high level as epics, which are later broken down into smaller stories.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> A use case is a process model that describes system-user interactions through a textual narrative to achieve a specific goal, encompassing normal, alternative, and exception flows for various scenarios. It plays a crucial role in transitioning from business to stakeholder or solution requirements by providing a detailed elaboration of interactions. They are essential for identifying both functional and non-functional requirements and for establishing acceptance criteria.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> SWOT analysis is a technique for analyzing the (S) strengths and (W) weaknesses of an organization or project, and the (O) opportunities and (T) threats that exist externally. SWOT analysis can be used to identify potential product risks in the form of positive risks (opportunities) or negative risks (threats).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Wireframes align the project team and business stakeholders with the system requirements during initial planning. They are low-fidelity drawings that illustrate the key elements and layout of the user interface, demonstrating how the system functions by walking through different screens of the application.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Story mapping is a technique for sequencing user stories based on their business value and the typical user sequence. It helps teams gain a shared understanding of the product to be built and communicates the features and components to be delivered. Initially, stories may be written at a high level as epics, which are later broken down into smaller stories. Option A: A use case is a process model that describes system-user interactions through a textual narrative to achieve a specific goal, encompassing normal, alternative, and exception flows for various scenarios. It plays a crucial role in transitioning from business to stakeholder or solution requirements by providing a detailed elaboration of interactions. They are essential for identifying both functional and non-functional requirements and for establishing acceptance criteria. Option C: SWOT analysis is a technique for analyzing the (S) strengths and (W) weaknesses of an organization or project, and the (O) opportunities and (T) threats that exist externally. SWOT analysis can be used to identify potential product risks in the form of positive risks (opportunities) or negative risks (threats). Option D: Wireframes align the project team and business stakeholders with the system requirements during initial planning. They are low-fidelity drawings that illustrate the key elements and layout of the user interface, demonstrating how the system functions by walking through different screens of the application.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":12,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">All stakeholders are attending a meeting to discuss a new project that is expected to start within a month and to last for at least 10 iterations. One stakeholder suggests that someone should be responsible for developing and maintaining the product roadmap. Who should assume this responsibility?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"All stakeholders are attending a meeting to discuss a new project that is expected to start within a month and to last for at least 10 iterations. One stakeholder suggests that someone should be responsible for developing and maintaining the product roadmap. Who should assume this responsibility?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project Manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project Manager\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Development Team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Development Team\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Scrum Master<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Scrum Master\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Product Owner<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Product Owner\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">In agile, the product owner should be in charge of managing the product roadmap since they are responsible for the product’s success. The Product Owner’s primary responsibility is to represent the business, which involves the creation and maintenance of the Product Vision and Roadmap, as well as the Product Backlog.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D In agile, the product owner should be in charge of managing the product roadmap since they are responsible for the product’s success. The Product Owner’s primary responsibility is to represent the business, which involves the creation and maintenance of the Product Vision and Roadmap, as well as the Product Backlog.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":13,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Which of the following elements are included in the business case? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following elements are included in the business case? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Situation statement<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Situation statement\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business goals and objectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Business goals and objectives\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Feasibility study results<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Feasibility study results\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder analysis\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Risk management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Risk management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A, B, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A situation statement is an objective summary of a problem or opportunity,  explaining its effect on the organization and its impact. It is part of the business case and helps reviewers understand the challenge before evaluating potential solutions. It is the output of the \\\"identify problem or opportunity\\\" process.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\">Business goals and objectives define the specific outcomes a portfolio, program, or project is expected to achieve, they are the output of of the “determine future state” process and focus on targeted business outcomes Feasibility study results are the summarized findings from the feasibility analysis, compiled into a package to aid executive review and decision-making. Feasibility study results are the output of the process “determine viable options and provide recommendation”. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 96)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Options D &amp; E:<\\/span> Stakeholder analysis and Risk management plan are done after the approval of the project; during the project planning phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, B, C A situation statement is an objective summary of a problem or opportunity,  explaining its effect on the organization and its impact. It is part of the business case and helps reviewers understand the challenge before evaluating potential solutions. It is the output of the \\\"identify problem or opportunity\\\" process. Business goals and objectives define the specific outcomes a portfolio, program, or project is expected to achieve, they are the output of of the “determine future state” process and focus on targeted business outcomes Feasibility study results are the summarized findings from the feasibility analysis, compiled into a package to aid executive review and decision-making. Feasibility study results are the output of the process “determine viable options and provide recommendation”. (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 96) Options D & E: Stakeholder analysis and Risk management plan are done after the approval of the project; during the project planning phase.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":14,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">A new project manager has just been assigned to oversee a stopped project. To quickly get accustomed to the project's processes and understand the scope of work, which tool would be the most effective?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A new project manager has just been assigned to oversee a stopped project. To quickly get accustomed to the project's processes and understand the scope of work, which tool would be the most effective?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Process flow diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Process flow diagram\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Retrospectives and lessons learned<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Retrospectives and lessons learned\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Persona analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Persona analysis\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>RACI Model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. RACI Model\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A process flow visually outlines the steps or tasks involved in job functions or interactions with a product. It forms the foundation for training materials on new procedures and may include additional flows to detail the transition processes, helping the project manager understand what needs to be done.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Retrospectives and lessons learned leverage past experiences to enhance future planning. Effective stakeholder engagement and communication strategies often incorporate recommendations and successful practices from previous projects or iterations to improve product development efforts. It’s an incorrect answer in this case as it’s not a designed tool for overviewing project processes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A persona is a fictional character that represents an individual or group of stakeholders. By analyzing these personas, patterns can emerge that help identify effective strategies for engaging and communicating with them.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The RACI model is a responsibility assignment matrix that clarifies stakeholder involvement by designating roles as Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, and Informed. It helps portfolio, program, or project managers define roles and responsibilities, reducing confusion and conflicts, particularly in overlapping responsibilities<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A A process flow visually outlines the steps or tasks involved in job functions or interactions with a product. It forms the foundation for training materials on new procedures and may include additional flows to detail the transition processes, helping the project manager understand what needs to be done. Option B: Retrospectives and lessons learned leverage past experiences to enhance future planning. Effective stakeholder engagement and communication strategies often incorporate recommendations and successful practices from previous projects or iterations to improve product development efforts. It’s an incorrect answer in this case as it’s not a designed tool for overviewing project processes. Option C: A persona is a fictional character that represents an individual or group of stakeholders. By analyzing these personas, patterns can emerge that help identify effective strategies for engaging and communicating with them. Option D: The RACI model is a responsibility assignment matrix that clarifies stakeholder involvement by designating roles as Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, and Informed. It helps portfolio, program, or project managers define roles and responsibilities, reducing confusion and conflicts, particularly in overlapping responsibilities\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":15,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Which of the following includes functional and non-functional requirements?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following includes functional and non-functional requirements?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Business requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Business requirements\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholders requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Stakeholders requirements\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Solution requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Solution requirements\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transition requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Transition requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Solution requirements outline the specific attributes of a solution, including the features and functionalities of a product. These requirements address both business and stakeholder needs and must be detailed enough to guide the design and development of the solution effectively. Solution requirements have two subcategories: functional and non-functional requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Business requirements outline the high-level needs and objectives of the organization, including key issues or opportunities that the project aims to address. They provide a rationale for undertaking the project, typically articulated through a business case that highlights the anticipated benefits and strategic value<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Stakeholder requirements outline the specific needs and expectations of individual stakeholders or stakeholder groups.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Transition requirements describe the procedures for deploying and releasing a solution into production. These requirements are specific to the deployment phase and are temporary; they will not need to be executed again once the project is complete.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Solution requirements outline the specific attributes of a solution, including the features and functionalities of a product. These requirements address both business and stakeholder needs and must be detailed enough to guide the design and development of the solution effectively. Solution requirements have two subcategories: functional and non-functional requirements. Option A: Business requirements outline the high-level needs and objectives of the organization, including key issues or opportunities that the project aims to address. They provide a rationale for undertaking the project, typically articulated through a business case that highlights the anticipated benefits and strategic value . Option B: Stakeholder requirements outline the specific needs and expectations of individual stakeholders or stakeholder groups. Option D: Transition requirements describe the procedures for deploying and releasing a solution into production. These requirements are specific to the deployment phase and are temporary; they will not need to be executed again once the project is complete.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":16,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-1\\\">Which tool or technique is part of defining acceptance criteria?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which tool or technique is part of defining acceptance criteria?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>PERT Charts<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. PERT Charts\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>SWOT Analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. SWOT Analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Behavior-driven Developmen<span><\\/span>t<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Behavior-driven Developmen t\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk Register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Risk Register\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Behavior-driven Development (BDD) involves defining acceptance criteria through a collaborative process, ensuring that conditions are clear and measurable through user stories and scenarios (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 218 &amp; 219).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> PERT (Program Evaluation Review Technique) is a scheduling tool used to analyze the tasks required to complete a project, estimate time durations, and organize dependencies between tasks. It is not related to defining acceptance criteria, which focuses on conditions that a solution must meet to be accepted.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> SWOT (Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats) is a strategic planning tool used to evaluate these four aspects of a project or business. It helps in understanding the internal and external factors that affect a project but does not directly contribute to defining acceptance criteria​<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A risk register is used to document risks, their impact, probability, and mitigation strategies. It helps in managing project risks but does not play a role in defining acceptance criteria for a solution<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Behavior-driven Development (BDD) involves defining acceptance criteria through a collaborative process, ensuring that conditions are clear and measurable through user stories and scenarios (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, pages 218 & 219). Option A: PERT (Program Evaluation Review Technique) is a scheduling tool used to analyze the tasks required to complete a project, estimate time durations, and organize dependencies between tasks. It is not related to defining acceptance criteria, which focuses on conditions that a solution must meet to be accepted. Option B: SWOT (Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, and Threats) is a strategic planning tool used to evaluate these four aspects of a project or business. It helps in understanding the internal and external factors that affect a project but does not directly contribute to defining acceptance criteria Option D: A risk register is used to document risks, their impact, probability, and mitigation strategies. It helps in managing project risks but does not play a role in defining acceptance criteria for a solution\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":17,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sTU-0\\\">A business analyst was assigned to an airline reservation system. The business analyst used the following artifact to illustrate the interactions with the system. What artifact did the business analyst use?<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_sFS-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst was assigned to an airline reservation system. The business analyst used the following artifact to illustrate the interactions with the system. What artifact did the business analyst use?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use case diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Use case diagram\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Flowchart diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Flowchart diagram\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>User interface flow<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. User interface flow\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Data flow diagram<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Data flow diagram\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Use case diagrams are used to identify the list of both the users of the solution and the possible scenarios of how each user will use the solution (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 206).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Use case diagrams are used to identify the list of both the users of the solution and the possible scenarios of how each user will use the solution (The PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 206).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":18,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A retail has recently experienced a 20% drop in online sales. What is the first step a business analyst would take?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A retail has recently experienced a 20% drop in online sales. What is the first step a business analyst would take?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Implement a new marketing strategy<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Implement a new marketing strategy\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Gather data on customer behavior and website performance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Gather data on customer behavior and website performance\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interview stakeholders to identify internal inefficiencies<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Interview stakeholders to identify internal inefficiencies\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hire an external stakeholder to investigate the cause<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Hire an external stakeholder to investigate the cause\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">The business analyst needs to understand the current situation before determining the causes of the problem. Data collection allows for an evidence-based analysis of potential issues related to the user experience, website functionality, and customer trends, providing a foundation for future steps.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Implementing a new marketing strategy is a solution-oriented action that should not be the first step.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> While interviewing stakeholders is important, the issue at hand involves online sales. It is more appropriate to first gather data on customer behavior.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Hiring an external stakeholder to investigate the cause can be an option later in the process if internal efforts do not yield results, but it should not be the first step<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The business analyst needs to understand the current situation before determining the causes of the problem. Data collection allows for an evidence-based analysis of potential issues related to the user experience, website functionality, and customer trends, providing a foundation for future steps. Option A: Implementing a new marketing strategy is a solution-oriented action that should not be the first step. Option C: While interviewing stakeholders is important, the issue at hand involves online sales. It is more appropriate to first gather data on customer behavior. Option D: Hiring an external stakeholder to investigate the cause can be an option later in the process if internal efforts do not yield results, but it should not be the first step .\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":19,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">A product manager is pushing for the development of a new feature in an existing app. However, the business analyst has concerns that this feature may not address the core problem. What should the business analyst do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A product manager is pushing for the development of a new feature in an existing app. However, the business analyst has concerns that this feature may not address the core problem. What should the business analyst do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Move forward with the feature development since the manager has requested it.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Move forward with the feature development since the manager has requested it.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Collaborate with the development team to begin testing the new feature.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Collaborate with the development team to begin testing the new feature.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Proceed with the feature development while documenting the concerns for future reference<span><\\/span>.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Proceed with the feature development while documenting the concerns for future reference .\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Pause development and conduct a root cause analysis to ensure the right problem is being addressed.<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Pause development and conduct a root cause analysis to ensure the right problem is being addressed.\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-0\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-0\\\">Pausing development and conducting a root cause analysis ensures that the business analyst properly investigates the underlying issue before moving forward with the solution.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Moving forward with the feature development overlooks the business analyst's responsibility to ensure that the solution addresses the actual problem, which can lead to wasted resources if the feature doesn't resolve the core issue.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Testing without first ensuring the feature is the correct solution is premature. It can further divert resources away from identifying the real problem.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-1\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> While documenting concerns is helpful, proceeding with development without addressing the core issue can still result in an ineffective solution.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Pausing development and conducting a root cause analysis ensures that the business analyst properly investigates the underlying issue before moving forward with the solution. Option A: Moving forward with the feature development overlooks the business analyst's responsibility to ensure that the solution addresses the actual problem, which can lead to wasted resources if the feature doesn't resolve the core issue. Option B: Testing without first ensuring the feature is the correct solution is premature. It can further divert resources away from identifying the real problem. Option C: While documenting concerns is helpful, proceeding with development without addressing the core issue can still result in an ineffective solution.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":20,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sTU-0\\\">Match the correct scenario to the appropriate process:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,";
